# OVERRIDE repository structure

What every folder is for, who owns it, and where new files go. If this file and `.github/CODEOWNERS`
ever disagree, CODEOWNERS is what GitHub enforces: fix whichever one is wrong in a pull request.

**Owners:** Shajeeve (World Builder, Director) · Gunitha (Systems Engineer, Hunter) ·
Ilzam (Core Developer, Duelist) · Rithish (Agent Controller, Pathfinder)

**Buddies (reviewers):** Shajeeve ↔ Rithish · Gunitha ↔ Ilzam

---

## 1. Top level

| Path | What it is for | Primary owner | In Git as | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Assets/` | Everything Unity imports | See Section 2 | Normal + LFS | Only `_Project/` and `ThirdParty/` are ours to organise |
| `Assets/_Project/` | All work made by the team | See Section 2 | Normal + LFS | Underscore keeps it at the top of the Project window |
| `Assets/ThirdParty/` | Imported CC0 packs (textures, sounds) | Whoever imports it | Normal + LFS | Add every pack to the Third-party table in `README.md` with source and licence |
