## 2. `Assets/_Project/`

### Scripts

Each area has its own assembly (`.asmdef`). An assembly can only use code from the assemblies listed
in "May use". This is what keeps AI brains separate from visuals (IS rubric: gameplay integration).

| Folder | Assembly | May use | What goes here | Primary owner | Reviewer |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Scripts/Core/` | `Override.Core` | nothing | Shared contracts: `WorldSnapshot`, `AgentCommand`, `IAgentBrain`; `NoiseEvent` type; blackboard; shared interfaces such as `IDamageable` | Rithish (contracts steward) | Shajeeve |
| `Scripts/AI/Director/` | `Override.AI` | Core | Director brain: simulated annealing over spawn and door-lock plans, tension score | Shajeeve | Rithish |
| `Scripts/AI/Hunter/` | `Override.AI` | Core | Seeker brain: Bayesian belief grid, its own grid A*, lure logic | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/AI/Duelist/` | `Override.AI` | Core | Warden brain: depth-2 Expectimax, evaluation function, player-habit learning | Ilzam | Gunitha |
| `Scripts/AI/Pathfinder/` | `Override.AI` | Core | Wisp brain: exposure-weighted A*, destination prediction, ambush choice | Rithish | Shajeeve |
| `Scripts/AI/Navigation/` | `Override.AI` | Core | Waypoint graph data structure and graph A* used by the Pathfinder | Rithish | Shajeeve |
| `Scripts/Sensors/` | `Override.Sensors` | Core | Vision (field of view + two raycasts) and hearing; post sightings to the blackboard | Ilzam | Gunitha |
| `Scripts/Motor/` | `Override.Motor` | Core | Turns `AgentCommand` into movement, rotation, hover motion and Animator parameters | Rithish | Shajeeve |
| `Scripts/Player/Controller/` | `Override.Player` | Core, Input System | Movement, first-person camera, sprint, crouch, jump | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/Player/Weapon/` | `Override.Player` | Core, Input System | Rifle: raycast, recoil, spread, reload, ammo, hit markers, procedural sway and reload motion | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/Player/Health/` | `Override.Player` | Core, Input System | Health and damage for the player **and** enemies | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/Player/Interaction/` | `Override.Player` | Core, Input System | Doors, crate barricades, scrap-canister throwable | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/Player/Noise/` | `Override.Player` | Core, Input System | Noise emitters (footsteps, shots, doors, crates, canister) | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/Level/` | `Override.Level` | Core | Markup components (waypoint, cover point, spawn point, zone volume, Seeker start, Warden guard post); zone lighting switch | Shajeeve | Rithish |
| `Scripts/Gameplay/` | `Override.Gameplay` | Core, AI, Sensors, Motor, Player, Level | The glue: terminals and hacking, game state, defence-wave trigger, respawn, alarm level, building the `WorldSnapshot`, ticking brains | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/UI/` | `Override.UI` | Core, Player, Gameplay, TextMeshPro | HUD (health, ammo, crosshair, alarm, hack progress), menus | Gunitha | Ilzam |
| `Scripts/DebugOverlay/` | `Override.DebugOverlay` | Core, AI, Input System | F1 toggle and overlay host; each agent owner adds their own panel | **Not yet assigned** (see Section 6) | — |

Dependency flow:

```
Player/Interaction ──(NoiseEvent, door/crate state)──┐
Sensors ──(sightings, heard noises)──────────────────┤
Level markup ──(waypoints, cover, spawns, zones)─────┤
                                                      ▼
                              WorldSnapshot      (Scripts/Core)
                                                      ▼
                         IAgentBrain.Tick()      (Scripts/AI, plain C#)
                                                      ▼
                              AgentCommand       (Scripts/Core)
                                                      ▼
                Motor → movement, rotation, Animator  (Scripts/Motor)
```

Two points that often confuse people:

- **`NoiseEvent` lives in `Core`, but Gunitha writes it.** Sensors and AI must read it without
  depending on Player code. Gunitha adds it through a pull request that Rithish approves.
- **The Hunter's A\* is not the Navigation A\*.** The Seeker searches a 2 m grid; the Wisps search the
  waypoint graph. Each owner keeps their own search in their own agent folder.

