## 5. Where does it go?

| I am adding… | Put it in | Remember |
|---|---|---|
| A new C# script | The `Scripts/` folder for its area | One class per file; file name = class name |
| A number someone may tune | A ScriptableObject in `Data/<area>/` | Never hard-code it |
| A model | `.blend` in `ArtSource/<Model>/`, FBX in `Art/Models/<Model>/` | Commit each modelling stage |
| A texture | `Art/Textures/Environment/` or `Art/Textures/Props/` | 2K max environment, 1K max props |
| A CC0 asset pack | `Assets/ThirdParty/<PackName>/` | Add it to the README licence table |
| Something to test alone | Your sandbox scene | Hand over a prefab, not scene edits |
| Something for the real level | A prefab, then ask Shajeeve to place it in `Main.unity` | Only Shajeeve edits the main scene |
| A profiler capture | Screenshot in `Docs/Evidence/<Name>/` | Raw `.data` files stay out of Git |
| A change to `WorldSnapshot`, `AgentCommand` or `IAgentBrain` | `Scripts/Core/` through a pull request | Rithish must approve |

Moving or renaming anything inside `Assets/`: do it **inside Unity**, not in File Explorer, so the
`.meta` file moves with it. Commit the `.meta` changes too.

